Mix.Compilers.Protocol: consolidate the protocols of Elixir in the lib directory of OTP

The consolidation skips each code path in the lib directory of OTP. In
one file with OTP and Elixir (beam.com), the applications of Elixir are
in that directory too, so Mix did not consolidate String.Chars,
Enumerable, Inspect and the other protocols of Elixir for a project.

Keep the code paths of the applications of Elixir. In a usual install,
Elixir is not in the lib directory of OTP, so nothing changes there.

--- a/lib/mix/lib/mix/compilers/protocol.ex
+++ b/lib/mix/lib/mix/compilers/protocol.ex
@@ -132,8 +132,17 @@
   defp consolidation_paths do
     otp = :code.lib_dir()
 
+    # The applications of Elixir can be in the lib directory of OTP, as in
+    # one file with both (beam.com). Their protocols are consolidated too.
+    elixir =
+      for app <- [:elixir, :eex, :ex_unit, :iex, :logger, :mix],
+          dir <- [:code.lib_dir(app)],
+          is_list(dir),
+          do: dir
+
     # Pre-list the paths in each directory for performance
-    for path <- :code.get_path(), not :lists.prefix(otp, path) do
+    for path <- :code.get_path(),
+        not :lists.prefix(otp, path) or Enum.any?(elixir, &:lists.prefix(&1, path)) do
       {path,
        case :file.list_dir(path) do
          {:ok, files} -> files
